{:adr/id 12
 :adr/status :accepted-defective
 :decision :call-clobber-linear-scan
 :supersedes {:adr/id 6 :scope :control-flow-all-vregs}
 :contract {:mir/version 3
            :straight-line-policy :call-live
            :control-flow-policy :linear-scan-preserved-across-calls
            :fallback-policy :all-vregs
            :call-clobbers :caller-saved
            :live-across-preference :preserved-tier
            :spill-placement :at-definition
            :reload-at-block-entry :backed-values}
 ;; Measured 2026-08-18 through amu, which executes native code. This
 ;; implementation returns wrong answers. The decision is not withdrawn; the
 ;; implementation is not safe to consume.
 ;;
 ;;   amu on 8872a54 (before this ADR): 1094 tests, 0 failures
 ;;   amu on 7f7c556 (this ADR):        1096 tests, 62 failures
 ;;
 ;; 60 of them are string search, split 30 AArch64 / 30 x86-64. An even split
 ;; across two independent encoders puts the fault in this shared allocator.
 ;;
 ;;   (defn main [] (if (string-contains? "abcdef" "def") 1 0))  => 0
 ;;
 ;; `string-replace-all` returns wrong content and wrong byte lengths, and one
 ;; multi-byte case traps. Cases expecting "absent" largely still pass, so the
 ;; search loop fails to FIND rather than failing outright.
 ;;
 ;; Partial cause, confirmed. `last-uses` records the highest instruction INDEX
 ;; at which a vreg is a source; it reads no label and no branch target. That
 ;; was sound while this scanner only saw straight-line functions, where
 ;; textual order is execution order. Routing control flow to it lets a back
 ;; edge re-read a value whose interval has ended.
 ;;
 ;; `back-edge?` now sends call-containing functions with a backward
 ;; `:mir/jump` or `:mir/branch-zero` to all-vreg. That is necessary and NOT
 ;; sufficient, measured rather than assumed:
 ;;
 ;;   without it: 62 failures   with it: 61 failures
 ;;
 ;; It fixes `let-composes-with-recursion-within-the-fuel-budget` and does not
 ;; touch string search at all -- so whatever loop `string-contains?` and
 ;; `string-replace-all` lower to is not a backward jump this predicate sees,
 ;; and the remaining fault is not yet located. Do not read the predicate as
 ;; the fix.
 ;;
 ;; Shapes that are correct, so the defect is narrower than "calls plus
 ;; control flow": call + `if` with 10 values live across the call; two calls
 ;; with the first result live across the second; a call result used directly
 ;; as a branch condition; kernel_call_branch and kernel_call_deep_branch.
 :defect {:since "7f7c55691697ba25abf6d732870a159433ce1fab"
          :reproducer "(defn main [] (if (string-contains? \"abcdef\" \"def\") 1 0))"
          :expected 1
          :actual 0
          :downstream "amu: 62 failures (60 string search, 30 per ISA)"
          :also #{:string-replace-all-wrong-content
                  :string-replace-all-wrong-byte-length
                  :multi-byte-case-traps}
          :partial-cause #{:textual-last-use-across-a-back-edge
                           :reload-in-one-arm-keeps-assigned-for-the-other}
          :partial-fix {:predicate :back-edge?
                        :fixes #{:let-composes-with-recursion-within-the-fuel-budget}
                        :does-not-fix #{:string-contains? :string-replace-all}
                        :measured "62 failures -> 61"}
          :partial-fix-2 {:drop-backed-at-label true
                          :encoding-test :v3-else-arm-reloads-a-value-the-then-arm-already-reloaded
                          :amu-measured false}
          :not-yet-located "string search loop still unmeasured after sibling-arm reload drop"
          :invisible-to #{"kotoba-mir suite" "kotoba-native suite"}
          :why-invisible "neither repository executes a compiled program"
          :do-not "advance amu onto this pin until string-contains? is measured green"}
 :fallbacks #{:register-pressure}
 :claims {:cfg-liveness false
          :spill-slot-coloring false
          :rust-performance-parity false
          :llvm-beaten false}}
